{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And HaShem would speak… face to face.</b> The intention here is: according to the measure of preparation that Moses would make for receiving the countenance of the Shekhinah, to that same measure would be the apprehension from the supernal faces — for according to the degree that a person prepares himself for the influx of holiness, so will he attain." "And its saying <b>as a man speaks to his fellow</b> may be explained according to our way along the lines of the verse (Proverbs 27:19): ״כַּמַּיִם הַפָּנִים לַפָּנִים כֵּן לֵב הָאָדָם לָאָדָם״ — meaning, that hearts perceive in the hidden realm whether to love or to hate, for according to the degree that a person prepares his heart to love his fellow, so will his fellow's heart be moved to love him in return. And that is what it means by <b>as a man speaks to his fellow</b> — that He would not love him unless he prepares his heart to be His fellow as well; so too HaShem spoke to him face to face. From this a person may discern what his standing is with his Maker — if his heart yearns and longs for HaShem and for His service, this is a sign that HaShem loves him."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:21.402868848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}